.TH XD\-COLOR 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-color \- Color Management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-color
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-color
is Color Management (Control Panel), after Windows 7's; Windows XP had the
same choices on a Color Management tab in a monitor's and a printer's
properties.
It is a client of colord, which keeps the devices, the ICC profiles and
which profile each device uses.
.TP
.B Devices
A device (monitors, printers, scanners, cameras), the profiles associated
with it, the default first; Add... associates an installed profile or,
with Browse..., a file; Remove and Set as Default Profile.
.TP
.B All Profiles
Every profile colord knows; Add... installs a file, and Remove uninstalls
one installed here (it goes to the Recycle Bin).
.PP
colord finds printers and scanners itself; the monitors the compositor
has are registered by
.B xd\-color
(with the device ids gnome-settings-daemon uses).
Profiles are copied into the user's profile store and handed to colord,
and the store's profiles are handed to it again at start, as colord
forgets them when it restarts.
.PP
A monitor's default profile is written to
.IR desktop.ini ,
from which
.BR xd\-compositor (1)
loads its calibration curves (vcgt) into the monitor's gamma ramp.
A default set by another program (colormgr) reaches the compositor the
next time
.B xd\-color
is opened.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on tab
.IR n :
0 (Devices) or 1 (All Profiles).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/icc/
The user's profile store (default
.IR ~/.local/share/icc ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/desktop.ini
.BR [ColorProfiles] :
each monitor's profile, by its key in
.IR monitors.ini .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-desk (1),
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR colormgr (1)
